\details{
The function inserts text into the current selection of a Word document.
Character input is inserted directly, while other objects are first converted
to text using an internal capture mechanism.

Formatting options such as paragraph style, font, and bullet lists can be
applied via method-specific arguments.

\code{TMod} tables: the coefficients and, separated by a rule,
the model statistics, all model columns aligned at the decimal point.
The header of the first column is \code{rowtitle}.

\code{TOne} tables (\code{DescToolsX::tOne()}): the column header
\code{"var"} is left empty, the group columns are right aligned and the
p-values aligned at the decimal point.

Tables: a 1-dimensional table is written as one column of
frequencies, a 2-dimensional one like a matrix, higher dimensions are
flattened with \code{ftable()} first.
}
